WEBVTT

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:02.935
Welcome to Homlle manual handling awareness.

00:00:03.155 --> 00:00:05.577
Moving equipment or supplies can cause injury

00:00:05.577 --> 00:00:07.654
when the task is not planned.

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:11.083
First consider whether hazardous handling can be avoided.

00:00:11.303 --> 00:00:13.369
If it cannot, assess the task

00:00:13.369 --> 00:00:15.435
and reduce the risk before starting.

00:00:15.655 --> 00:00:18.949
This lesson is not a practical lifting qualification.

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:23.957
The Manual Handling Operations Regulations 1992 set the

00:00:23.957 --> 00:00:28.135
Great Britain approach: avoid hazardous handling where reasonably

00:00:28.135 --> 00:00:32.312
practicable, assess what remains and reduce injury risk.

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:36.017
This includes carrying, pushing and pulling, not only lifting.

00:00:36.237 --> 00:00:39.255
Training alone cannot make an unsafe task safe.

00:00:39.475 --> 00:00:41.874
Northern Ireland has its own equivalent framework,

00:00:41.874 --> 00:00:44.273
which must be checked for work there.

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:48.851
Use four prompts: task, individual, load and environment.

00:00:49.071 --> 00:00:50.899
How often will you move it?

00:00:51.119 --> 00:00:53.285
Can you do so comfortably today?

00:00:53.505 --> 00:00:56.325
Is it awkward, unstable or hard to grip?

00:00:56.545 --> 00:00:58.680
Is the route clear and well lit?

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:01.172
Report pain, fatigue or restrictions privately

00:01:01.172 --> 00:01:03.443
so the work can be adjusted.

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:05.513
There is no single legal safe

00:01:05.513 --> 00:01:07.363
weight for every person and task.

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:11.686
Look at the load, grip, route, stairs and available space.

00:01:11.906 --> 00:01:14.036
Think about how often you must move

00:01:14.036 --> 00:01:15.862
it and your own capability today.

00:01:16.082 --> 00:01:19.078
There is no single weight that makes every lift safe.

00:01:19.298 --> 00:01:21.115
A light awkward item on a

00:01:21.115 --> 00:01:22.933
wet staircase may still be unsafe.

00:01:23.153 --> 00:01:25.563
Pause if the conditions are unsuitable.

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:28.918
Can you split supplies into smaller loads,

00:01:28.918 --> 00:01:31.094
use suitable equipment or arrange help?

00:01:31.314 --> 00:01:33.541
Clear the route before moving anything and

00:01:33.541 --> 00:01:35.451
check that the destination is ready.

00:01:35.671 --> 00:01:38.731
Help is useful only when the task is planned together.

00:01:38.951 --> 00:01:41.227
Do not use a customer as an

00:01:41.227 --> 00:01:43.504
unplanned lifting assistant for an unsafe task.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:46.296
Follow the handling method you have been

00:01:46.296 --> 00:01:48.311
shown for the actual task and equipment.

00:01:48.531 --> 00:01:52.263
Keep movements controlled and avoid sudden twisting or jerking.

00:01:52.483 --> 00:01:55.141
If the load shifts, the route becomes unsafe

00:01:55.141 --> 00:01:57.799
or you feel pain, stop safely and reassess.

00:01:58.019 --> 00:02:01.238
Do not push through discomfort to finish a booking faster.

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:04.857
For a load already assessed as manageable, plan where

00:02:04.857 --> 00:02:07.326
it will go and take a stable position.

00:02:07.546 --> 00:02:09.883
Get a secure grip and keep it close.

00:02:10.103 --> 00:02:13.118
Use a comfortable posture with some bending at the

00:02:13.118 --> 00:02:15.797
hips and knees, and move smoothly without jerking.

00:02:16.017 --> 00:02:17.898
Turn by moving your feet.

00:02:18.118 --> 00:02:20.869
Put it down before making a precise adjustment.

00:02:21.089 --> 00:02:23.340
Practise with a competent assessor.

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:26.747
A suitable trolley may reduce carrying, but

00:02:26.747 --> 00:02:28.947
pushing and pulling still need assessment.

00:02:29.167 --> 00:02:32.668
Check its condition, capacity, route and your view ahead.

00:02:32.888 --> 00:02:34.578
A heavy beauty case can become

00:02:34.578 --> 00:02:36.268
hard to control on a slope.

00:02:36.488 --> 00:02:39.515
Do not take ordinary wheeled equipment down stairs.

00:02:39.735 --> 00:02:41.771
Agree a suitable method or change

00:02:41.771 --> 00:02:43.468
the task before moving it.

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:46.339
A second person does not automatically

00:02:46.339 --> 00:02:48.054
make a difficult load safe.

00:02:48.274 --> 00:02:50.084
Team handling must be planned for

00:02:50.084 --> 00:02:51.895
the load, route and both people.

00:02:52.115 --> 00:02:53.755
Agree who gives the signal and

00:02:53.755 --> 00:02:55.122
where to put it down.

00:02:55.342 --> 00:02:57.476
Either person can stop the move.

00:02:57.696 --> 00:02:59.746
Do not ask an unprepared customer to

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:01.503
take part in a risky lift.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:04.758
Use suitable footwear and any grip

00:03:04.758 --> 00:03:06.823
protection identified by the assessment.

00:03:07.043 --> 00:03:09.773
PPE does not reduce the weight of a load.

00:03:09.993 --> 00:03:12.715
Repeated reaching, scrubbing and carrying can build

00:03:12.715 --> 00:03:15.047
up strain even with small items.

00:03:15.267 --> 00:03:19.757
Adjust equipment and work organisation, and report discomfort early.

00:03:19.977 --> 00:03:23.185
Pause an unsafe task instead of pushing through pain.

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:26.113
A customer may ask you to move a

00:03:26.113 --> 00:03:27.979
heavy sofa or help lift a person.

00:03:28.199 --> 00:03:30.170
These are not automatic additions to

00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:31.813
a cleaning or beauty booking.

00:03:32.033 --> 00:03:34.389
Do not attempt unassessed handling outside

00:03:34.389 --> 00:03:36.352
your competence and approved scope.

00:03:36.572 --> 00:03:39.207
Explain the boundary and contact support.

00:03:39.427 --> 00:03:42.774
Protecting safety must not cost you a positive rating.

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:45.590
Your equipment case is so full that

00:03:45.590 --> 00:03:47.600
it blocks your view on narrow stairs.

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:49.945
Should you carry it carefully anyway?

00:03:50.165 --> 00:03:51.240
No.

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:53.318
Stop and change the plan.

00:03:53.538 --> 00:03:55.857
Split the load if safe, clear the

00:03:55.857 --> 00:03:57.845
route or arrange another assessed method.

00:03:58.065 --> 00:04:00.283
Taking a little longer is better

00:04:00.283 --> 00:04:02.501
than accepting a foreseeable injury risk.

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:06.111
Complete the knowledge check, then demonstrate a

00:04:06.111 --> 00:04:08.943
safe representative task to a competent assessor.

00:04:09.163 --> 00:04:11.227
Explain when you would stop and how you

00:04:11.227 --> 00:04:13.033
would report a hazard or near miss.

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:16.207
Record the assessment against this lesson version.

00:04:16.427 --> 00:04:19.054
A completed video does not prove competence for

00:04:19.054 --> 00:04:21.353
every load, person or piece of equipment.

00:04:21.573 --> 00:04:24.393
Your assessor should check understanding, correct any

00:04:24.393 --> 00:04:27.214
gaps and observe the relevant practical skills.

00:04:27.434 --> 00:04:31.229
Do not treat video completion as automatic permission to work.
